  "slides": [
    {
      "page_title": "Interfaces, the Node Pattern & Union Basics",
      "blocks": [
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "text": "The Node Pattern"
        },
        {
          "type": "code",
          "lang": "graphql",
          "lines": [
            "interface Node { id: ID! }",
            "type User implements Node {",
            "  id: ID!",
            "  name: String!",
            "}",
            "type Query { node(id: ID!): Node }  # refetch"
          ],
          "note": "basis of Relay's normalized cache"
        },
        {
          "type": "bullets",
          "items": [
            "An implementer may tighten `String` → `String!` (==covariant==: same type, a subtype, or non-null)",
            "Loosening `String!` → `String` is **illegal**",
            "Apollo and Relay add `__typename` for you; their caches need it, so keep it on",
            "An interface with no implementers can never resolve"
          ],
          "ink": "red"
        },
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "text": "Union Basics"
        },
        {
          "type": "code",
          "lang": "graphql",
          "lines": [
            "union SearchResult = User | Post",
            "query S($q: String!) {",
            "  search(q: $q) { __typename",
            "    ... on User { name }",
            "    ... on Post { title } } }"
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "callout",
          "style": "tip",
          "title": "Same Runtime Duty",
          "text": "Like interfaces, a union needs server-side `resolveType` to map a runtime value onto a member type."
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "page_title": "Unions, Errors As Data & the Request Lifecycle",
      "blocks": [
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "text": "Union Or Interface"
        },
        {
          "type": "diagram",
          "kind": "cards",
          "spec": {
            "cards": [
              {
                "title": "`interface`",
                "lines": [
                  "Shared fields, \"is-a\"",
                  "Query common fields directly",
                  "Contract on implementers"
                ]
              },
              {
                "title": "`union`",
                "lines": [
                  "No shared fields, \"one-of\"",
                  "A fragment per member",
                  "Members stay unrelated"
                ]
              }
            ]
          }
        },
        {
          "type": "callout",
          "style": "takeaway",
          "title": "Growth Breaks Clients",
          "text": "Adding a member is breaking in practice: existing clients have no fragment for it and render an empty object. Ship a fallback branch and treat unknown `__typename` as a degraded render, not a crash."
        },
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "text": "Errors As Data"
        },
        {
          "type": "code",
          "lang": "graphql",
          "lines": [
            "union CreateUserResult =",
            "    CreateUserSuccess",
            "  | EmailTaken",
            "  | RateLimited"
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "bullets",
          "items": [
            "The `errors` array is untyped and loses non-null guarantees",
            "A result union keeps failure modes in schema and codegen",
            "Give members `interface Error { message: String! }`",
            "Clients then render any failure generically"
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "sidebox",
          "title": "Where Unions Fit",
          "items": [
            "Search results",
            "Feeds and activity streams",
            "Notification lists"
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "sidebox",
          "title": "No Input Unions",
          "items": [
            "The spec has no input union type",
            "Emulate with `@oneOf`: an input where exactly one field is set",
            "Many members force long brittle client queries",
            "Prefer an interface when types truly share fields"
          ],
          "ink": "red"
        },
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "text": "Request Lifecycle",
          "ink": "blue"
        },
        {
          "type": "diagram",
          "kind": "flow",
          "spec": {
            "nodes": [
              "parse to AST",
              "validate",
              "coerce variables",
              "execute",
              "format response"
            ]
          }
        },
        {
          "type": "bullets",
          "items": [
            "Parse and validation errors return before execution",
            "That response has `errors` and no `data` key at all",
            "A bad variable is a request-level error, not a field error"
          ]
        }
      ]
    }
  ],
  "caption": {
    "text": "Most GraphQL outages are not resolver bugs — they are schema decisions made in a hurry. Part 3 of GRAPHQL SCHEMA DESIGN covers the Node pattern and the rules for implementing an interface, unions and when to pick one over an interface, errors as data, and the request lifecycle from parse to response.",
